# large binary run checkpoints (kept on disk, not in git)
*.pkl

# macOS metadata.
# This repository is worked on from an exFAT volume, where macOS writes an
# AppleDouble sidecar ("._<name>", magic 00 05 16 07) beside essentially every
# file on every write. One cleanup pass removed 5,925 of them, 441 of those
# inside .git, where they made git emit "non-monotonic index" errors on every
# command.
#
# These patterns are ADVISORY: `git add -f` bypasses .gitignore entirely, and a
# file that is already tracked is never checked against it again. The hard block
# is .githooks/pre-commit, enabled per clone with:
#   git config core.hooksPath .githooks
._*
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
.LSOverride
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
__MACOSX/
Icon?
